cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HeadVox, please cite it as below."
title: "HeadVox: script to voiceover with word-aligned captions"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "HeadVox contributors"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-11-08
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yyert123/headvox"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/headvox/headvox"
abstract: >-
  HeadVox is an open-source Python CLI and library that turns a text or Markdown
  script into a neural text-to-speech voiceover with SRT/WebVTT captions aligned
  to the spoken words and a per-word JSON timing manifest, with optional ffmpeg
  video muxing. Supports Chinese, English and Japanese.
keywords:
  - text-to-speech
  - voiceover
  - subtitles
  - word-level timestamps
  - talking-head video
